   note:"GitHub's advisory database flagged 20 npm packages as malware (CWE-506) on October 28: dsh-redteam-mode, b20miner, @zaip-ai/cli, black-spindle, itsa-utils, itsa-react-checkbox, @walknpm/todo-cli, dsh-plugin-blender-3d, mock-transactions-sdk, transaction-info-generate-sdk, my-empty-package, camelotlabs-utils, camelotlabs-worker, camelotlabs-sdk, camelotlabs-config, camelotlabs-core, @atlisp/mcp, @testsecuiitytestme/cache-helper, csvflow-schema, @webapp-shared/login-vmok. Any machine that installed or ran one of them should be considered under outside control.",
