   note:"A Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability has been discovered in the CKEditor 5 engine. This vulnerability is caused by a prototype pollution issue in the es-toolkit library used in the CKEditor 5 codebase. This vulnerability could lead to unauthorized JavaScript code execution when the editor processes incoming style attribute values. GitHub rates it high (CVSS 8.1). 1 more advisory for ckeditor5 came out the same day.",
