   title:"libXtst: 3 CVEs fixed, the most serious rated critical",
   note:"It was discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain RECORD replies from the X server. A malicious X server could possibly use this issue to cause libXtst clients to crash, resulting in a denial of service. Tobias Stoeckmann discovered that libXtst did not properly handle certain memory operations. USN-8939-1 covers 3 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2016-7951 (Ubuntu priority low, CVSS 9.8). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2016-7952, CVE-2026-94286.",
   fix:"Fixed in libxtst 2:1.2.3-1ubuntu0.18.04.1~esm1 (18.04), libxtst 2:1.2.3-1ubuntu0.20.04.1~esm1 (20.04), libxtst 2:1.2.3-1ubuntu0.22.04.1 (22.04), libxtst 2:1.2.3-1.1ubuntu0.1 (24.04) and 3 more listed in USN-8939-1. In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
