   title:"Go: 12 CVEs fixed, the most serious rated critical",
   note:"It was discovered that Go did not enforce a maximum recursion depth when parsing deeply nested ASN.1 structures. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Go to crash, resulting in a denial of service. It was discovered that Go incorrectly reset the depth counter when decoding XML elements. USN-8935-1 covers 12 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2026-78663 (Ubuntu priority medium, CVSS 9.1). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2026-56865, CVE-2026-56866, CVE-2026-94439, CVE-2026-33818, CVE-2026-78660.",
