   title:"PHP: 10 CVEs fixed, the most serious rated high",
   note:"It was discovered that PHP did not properly validate the size of MySQL server packets in the mysqlnd driver. A malicious server could possibly use this issue to cause PHP to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue was only addressed in Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.10. USN-8936-1 covers 10 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2026-91765 (Ubuntu priority medium, CVSS 7.5).",
