   note:"USN-8883-1 fixed a vulnerability in Go versions 1.18, 1.21, and 1.24. This update provides the corresponding fix for Go version 1.23. Original advisory details: It was discovered that the Go x/net/idna package incorrectly handled certain Punycode-encoded labels that decoded to ASCII-only labels. An attacker could possibly use this issue to bypass hostname-based access controls and escalate privileges. USN-8883-2 covers 1 CVE (Ubuntu priority high, CVSS 9.6).",
