   title:"RabbitMQ Server: 12 CVEs fixed, the most serious rated critical",
   note:"It was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled CORS wildcard origin configuration. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a cross-site request forgery attack. This issue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. It was discovered that RabbitMQ Server incorrectly handled TLS peer-certificate DNs in the management UI. USN-8933-1 covers 12 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2026-67237 (Ubuntu priority medium, CVSS 9.3). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2026-67231, CVE-2026-66070, CVE-2026-67232, CVE-2026-66079, CVE-2026-67404.",
