   note:"Stanislav Fort discovered that curl did not properly clear AWS SigV4 authentication state when CURLOPT_AWS_SIGV4 was set to NULL. An attacker could possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. USN-8932-1 covers 9 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2026-92388 (Ubuntu priority low, CVSS 9.1). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2026-86414, CVE-2026-92389, CVE-2026-87864, CVE-2026-87862, CVE-2026-87863.",
