   title:"FFmpeg: 8 CVEs fixed, the most serious rated high",
   note:"Momoko Shiraishi discovered that FFmpeg did not correctly handle certain memory operations. An attacker could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. It was discovered that FFmpeg did not correctly handle certain memory operations. USN-8915-1 covers 8 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2026-30754 (Ubuntu priority medium, CVSS 8.8). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2026-38350, CVE-2026-38348, CVE-2026-38346, CVE-2026-38347, CVE-2026-38344.",
