   note:"Timo Preißl discovered that U-Boot incorrectly handled certain malformed ZFS file system metadata. An attacker could possibly use this issue to trigger an integer overflow and out-of-bounds memory access, resulting in arbitrary code execution or a denial of service. Timo Preißl discovered that U-Boot incorrectly calculated buffer sizes when processing certain ext4 file systems. USN-8884-1 covers 4 CVEs; the most serious rated one is CVE-2025-70290 (Ubuntu priority medium, CVSS 9.8). Also rated high or critical: CVE-2025-70293, CVE-2026-71971.",
